<title>GREECE: EBRD drachma bond gets Athens bourse approval.</title>
<headline>EBRD drachma bond gets Athens bourse approval.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Athens stock exchange said in a statement it gave the green light to a five-year, 10.25 percent EBRD bond worth 20 billion drachmas.</p>
<p>The bond will be listed on the Athens bourse pending final approval from the capital markets commission. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
